  "final": "Done. The off-by-one-cent rows came from float math in `billing/totals.py`.\n\n`line_total_cents` multiplied prices as floats and then used Python's `round()`. A value that is exactly half a cent, like 1.005, is stored slightly below the tie, so it rounded down to 1.00. That contradicts the README, which says amounts are rounded half up.\n\nI switched the calculation to `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. 1.005 now gives 101 cents and 2.675 gives 268.\n\nI added a regression test, `test_half_up_exact_ties`. All 7 tests pass with the fix. With the old `totals.py` restored, the suite fails (`FAILED (failures=1)`).\n\nI didn't run it against your real CSV, so rows that were off for a different reason, if any, would still show up.",
